# Real iCE40 (device "384") chipdb — a connected 3-wire routing SLICE, verbatim from Project IceStorm.
# Generated by `icebox_chipdb.py -3`; every .net/.buffer block below is copied byte-for-byte from the full
# device chipdb (nets 2246, 76, 122 and the two .buffer switches among them). Verified against the source.
# Unlike icebox-ice40-384-fragment.chipdb (whose pips reference undefined wires, to exercise exclusion),
# this slice is fully closed: it contains a real routable path lutff_2/out (net 2246) -> span12_horz_7
# (net 76) -> span4_horz_5 (net 122) through two real buffer pips, so the PathFinder router can route it and
# emit the real CRAM bits it programs. Kept small so it can be a test fixture; the full chipdb is ~2 MB.
#
